====================================================================================================================
NULL CALIBRATION -- all methods on random halves of a homogeneous group
Result = MEAN over `runs` independent random partitions; *_sd is the across-run SD (chance spread).
Individual per-run metrics are saved to null_calibration_per_run.csv (not printed here).
Under H0: FPR@alpha ~= alpha  AND  hits_FDR05 ~= 0.  inflation = FPR@.05/0.05 (~1 good, >1 over-calls).
ks_D / ad_A2 / cvm_W2 = distance of the p-values to Uniform(0,1) (KS / Anderson-Darling /
  Cramer-von Mises), averaged over runs; 0 = perfectly uniform. See QQ-plots in plots/.
n_per_group = replicates per fake group for that arm (full half + fixed subsamples).
k_config = TOX kNN neighbourhood config (k_start _ k_max, step 1); NA for edgeR/limma.
Cohorts include the 4 cancer stages AND healthy (matched normals), across all 8 cancers.
